{"name":"White Rock","hex":"#d4cfb4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"White Rock","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the Bathurst council area, central eastern New South Wales, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/White_Rock"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wedding Cake Rock","blocks":[{"text":"Wedding Cake Rock, also known as White Rock, is a sandstone rock formation located in the Royal National Park near Bundeena in Sydney, New South Wales, Australia, accessible via the Royal National Park Coast Track. The rock is one of many formations that appear north of Marley Beach, and is suspended 25 metres (82 ft) above sea level. Wedding Cake Rock is noted for its scenic location and popularity with bushwalkers and tourists, as an attractive location for photography. Its reputation, however, was damaged after the landmark saw a sudden spike in popularity in 2015, and subsequently fell victim to vandalism. The rock was closed off from public access in May 2015 by the New South Wales National Parks and Wildlife Service, citing the dangerous behavior of recent visitors, and later, safety concerns, after a survey conducted the following month determined that the rock was unstable, and that it would collapse into the Tasman Sea within the next decade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Travellers_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock%2C_December_2014.jpg/330px-Travellers_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock%2C_December_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedding_Cake_Rock"},{"title":"White Rock Conservation Park","blocks":[{"text":"White Rock, a prominent pale-coloured rockface on a peak, is the major feature of interest of the White Rock Conservation Park, situated within the White Rock, Queensland (Ipswich) locality, Australia. It is also known as \"Nugum\" to the traditional owners, the Ugarapul people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Nugum_-_White_Rock_QLD.jpg/330px-Nugum_-_White_Rock_QLD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Rock_Conservation_Park"},{"title":"White Rock (album)","blocks":[{"text":"White Rock  is the second soundtrack album by English keyboardist Rick Wakeman, released in January 1977 by A&M Records. It was produced as the soundtrack to White Rock, a 1977 documentary film about the 1976 Winter Olympics held in Innsbruck, Austria."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/89/Rick_Wakeman_album_-_White_Rock_-_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Rock_(album)"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Travellers_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock%2C_December_2014.jpg/500px-Travellers_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock%2C_December_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Travellers_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock%2C_December_2014.jpg/1280px-Travellers_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock%2C_December_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Travellers_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock%2C_December_2014.jpg/500px-Travellers_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock%2C_December_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Visitors interacting with Wedding Cake Rock, pictured in December 2014, prior to the landmark’s closure to the public.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWedding_Cake_Rock%2C_December_2014.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Wedding_Cake_Rock_panorama%2C_September_2013.jpg/500px-Wedding_Cake_Rock_panorama%2C_September_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Wedding_Cake_Rock_panorama%2C_September_2013.jpg/1280px-Wedding_Cake_Rock_panorama%2C_September_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Wedding_Cake_Rock_panorama%2C_September_2013.jpg/500px-Wedding_Cake_Rock_panorama%2C_September_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Panoramic view of Wedding Cake Rock's surrounds. The sandstone composition of the rock is distinct from surrounding cliffs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWedding_Cake_Rock_panorama%2C_September_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Wedding_Cake_Rock_-_panoramio_%28edited%29.jpg/500px-Wedding_Cake_Rock_-_panoramio_%28edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Wedding_Cake_Rock_-_panoramio_%28edited%29.jpg/1280px-Wedding_Cake_Rock_-_panoramio_%28edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Wedding_Cake_Rock_-_panoramio_%28edited%29.jpg/500px-Wedding_Cake_Rock_-_panoramio_%28edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Southern view of part of the rock's structure in May 2016, showing visible signs of erosion underneath. Concerns about the rock's\n\nstability led to the landmark's closure by the NPWS the previous year.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWedding_Cake_Rock_-_panoramio_(edited).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Sunset_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock.jpg/500px-Sunset_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Sunset_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock.jpg/500px-Sunset_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sunset with a top view of Wedding Cake Rock in July 2017.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunset_at_Wedding_Cake_Rock.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Six_Mile_Creek_Boardwalk_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Six_Mile_Creek_Boardwalk_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Six_Mile_Creek_Boardwalk_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Six_Mile_Creek_Boardwalk_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Six_Mile_Creek_Boardwalk_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Six_Mile_Creek_Boardwalk_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Six Mile Creek Boardwalk, 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASix_Mile_Creek_Boardwalk_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Canonization_2014-The_Canonization_of_Saint_John_XXIII_and_Saint_John_Paul_II_%2814037015405%29.jpg/500px-Canonization_2014-The_Canonization_of_Saint_John_XXIII_and_Saint_John_Paul_II_%2